| # | Acceptance Criterion | Implementation | Verification | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Local worker = full PRD-057 spec (provider, runtime, artifact, capability/endpoint/hardware profile); same artifact under two runtimes is two workers | `registry_workers.rs`: `LOCAL_PROVIDER`, `LocalRuntimeKind`, `LocalEndpointConfig`, `LocalResourceProfileConfig`, `LocalWorkerConfig`; runtime is part of existing `canonical_spec_identity()` hash | `local_worker_tests` module (8 tests) | Complete |
| 2 | Runtime contract covers probes, load/cold-start, streaming, tool calls, structured output, context limits, cancellation, concurrency/queue depth, memory pressure, crashes/disappearance, usage, optional auth, behind PRD-058 | `local_runtime.rs` (`LocalChatClient`: probe, submit/streaming/tool-calls/structured-output/errors), `local_worker.rs` (`LocalInferenceAdapter` implements `InferenceAdapter`), `local_worker_runtime.rs` (reservations for concurrency/slots/model-loading, crash/disappearance resolution) | `local_runtime` 16 tests, `local_worker` agent 10 tests + 1 unit, `local_worker_runtime` daemon 10 unit + 3 integration | Complete |
| 3 | Endpoint model verified against registered artifact where possible; unverifiable → degraded worker routing can refuse | `LocalChatClient::verify_artifact` (Ollama digest match/mismatch/unverifiable; Unsloth always unverifiable); `LocalArtifactVerificationState` in storage | `artifact_digest_*` tests in `local_runtime.rs`, `artifact_verification_degrades_honestly_*` in agent tests | Complete |
| 4 | OpenAI-compatible endpoint = transport reuse only; each backend keeps own RuntimeId/capability profile/empirical identity | `local_runtime.rs` module doc + contract doc "OpenAI-compatible transport is reuse only"; `LocalRuntimeKind::{Ollama,Unsloth}` distinct `RUNTIME_ID`s | `runtime_id_reflects_the_configured_backend`, `unsloth_runtime_reports_its_own_runtime_id` | Complete |
| 5 | Local telemetry: typed timestamped observations incl. token categories/wall time/TTFT/tok-per-sec/load time/peak memory/utilization/retries/failures into PRD-051 ledger with full spec identity; no invented USD cost | Migration 057 `local_worker_telemetry` table (separate from `usage_observations`/`cost_estimates`, no cost column); `local_telemetry.rs` repo; `local_worker_runtime::persist_local_telemetry` | `local_telemetry` 5 tests; `telemetry_records_no_invented_cost_*`; `full_pipeline_*` daemon integration test | Complete |
| 6 | Energy recorded only when measurable; operator-allocation policies produce local-estimate amounts w/ policy id/version, measurements, assumptions, currency, period, provenance, estimated-authority label; never implicit, never mixed with invoices | Migration 057 `local_allocation_policies`/`local_allocation_estimates` (disabled by default, `CHECK` constraints for closed cost category/authority label); `record_allocation_estimate` fails closed unless explicitly enabled | `allocation_estimate_requires_an_explicitly_enabled_policy`, `allocation_estimates_never_mix_with_provider_cost_estimates_table` | Complete |
| 7 | Local execution consumes PRD-064 typed reservations (accelerator/system memory, inference slots, model-loading slots, exclusive-runtime, thermal/power where available); never knowingly exceed observed capacity | `local_worker_runtime.rs`: `execution_resource_requests`, `acquire_model_load_reservation`, reuses `ReservationRepository` unchanged | `unknown_capacity_refuses_by_default_*`, reservation tests, daemon integration tests | Complete |
| 8 | Managed vs. externally-shared capacity distinct; freshness/confidence; contention/pressure/revocation detected and recorded honestly, never masked; coexistence never guaranteed over non-exclusive capacity | `LocalCapacityClass`, `CapacityObservation`, `capacity_is_fresh`; `resolve_reservation` commits observed consumption (honest overrun) | `capacity_freshness_rejects_stale_observations`, `managed_and_externally_shared_capacity_are_distinct_classes`, `mid_run_memory_pressure_is_recorded_as_honest_overrun` | Complete |
| 9 | Unknown capacity fails per explicit policy, never invented; acquire/commit/release/expiry/crash-recovery follow PRD-064 lifecycle | `UnknownCapacityPolicy::{Refuse,SerializeConservatively}`; all resolution delegates to unmodified `ReservationRepository` | `unknown_capacity_*` tests; crash/cancellation/completion resolution tests | Complete |
| 10 | Endpoint trust explicit (loopback/LAN/remote, optional TLS/auth by external reference); local model gains no extra capability beyond PRD-058 sandbox | `classify_local_endpoint_trust`; non-loopback requires `auth_profile`; adapter has no tool-execution surface at all (only HTTP) | `endpoint_trust_classifies_loopback_lan_and_remote`, `non_loopback_endpoint_requires_auth_profile` | Complete |
| 11 | Weights/templates untrusted; template injection can't change tool authority; telemetry has no prompts/outputs/credentials | Contract doc "Security"; `LocalTelemetryRow` carries no text/prompt fields; loop's `validate_tool_call`/`ToolAuthorizer` unmodified and still gates everything | Schema (no text columns) + reused PRD-058 authorization tests (unchanged) | Complete |
| 12 | PRD-032 can compare local workers with other workers; unknown $ never ranks as zero/cheap; local-resource consumption is its own metric class | No cost field anywhere in local telemetry; existing `estimated_cost_microusd: Option` discipline untouched | Contract doc "Comparability"; schema separation itself is the enforcement | Complete |
| 13 | Deterministic fake-runtime tests: probes, load/cold-start, streaming, tool calls, structured output, concurrency/queue limits, memory-pressure refusals, crash/disappearance, artifact verification+degraded, reservation races, telemetry — no real execution, no network beyond loopback fakes | `wiremock`-backed tests in `local_runtime.rs`/`tests/local_worker.rs`; in-memory/file-SQLite reservation races and pressure/crash tests in `local_worker_runtime.rs` (daemon) and its integration tests | 16+10+1+10+3 = 40 new tests, all passing, all loopback-only | Complete |

