## Summary

**Files changed:**
- New: `docs/contracts/local-worker-runtime.md`, `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config/registry_workers.rs` (additions), `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/local_runtime.rs`, `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/local_worker.rs` + `tests/local_worker.rs`, `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/local_worker_runtime.rs` + `tests/local_worker_runtime.rs`, `crates/familiar-ai-storage/migrations/057_local_worker_telemetry.sql`, `crates/familiar-ai-storage/src/repos/local_telemetry.rs` — every file the PRD's `expected_files` named was created.
- Modified: module registration (`lib.rs` × 3), migration registry + updated test counts (`migrate.rs`), `repos/mod.rs`, and 8 pre-existing `RegistryWorkerConfig` struct-literal call sites mechanically updated for the new `local` field.
- Migration: version 057 (the reserved slot), owns two new table pairs — `local_worker_telemetry` and the disabled-by-default `local_allocation_policies`/`local_allocation_estimates` — entirely separate from the PRD-051 ledger.

**Deviation found and fixed mid-implementation:** my first validation pass required any `provider = "local"` worker to declare a PRD-063 `local` profile, but a pre-existing test used `provider = "local"` as a plain descriptive label for an unrelated Codex-harness worker. I narrowed the rule to be one-directional (declaring `local` requires `provider = "local"`; the reverse is not required) and documented why in both the code and the contract.

**Tests:** 40 new tests across 5 crates, all passing. Full workspace suite (`cargo test --workspace --no-default-features`, matching the project's own Docker test recipe) is green except one pre-existing, confirmed-unrelated flake (`familiar-ai-core::paths::tests::tmp_fallback_uses_new_identity`, an env-var-mutating test with no thread isolation — passes cleanly alone; I never touched `paths.rs`). `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo clippy -D warnings` are clean on every file I touched; the one clippy warning in the workspace (`bootstrap.rs`) is pre-existing and untouched by me.

**Note on scope:** per the PRD's own Phasing section, this delivers Phase 1 (externally managed `ollama`/`unsloth` endpoints) plus the Phase 2 scheduling mechanism (reservations, capacity classes). Process-managed lifecycle and additional backends are explicitly out of scope, matching the PRD.

`git status` is clean aside from the tracked changes above; `docs/prds/PRD-063.md` has been moved to `docs/prds/done/` per repo convention.
