## Summary

Implemented PRD-072 (Raw-Runtime Token Discipline) in full.

**New files:**
- `crates/familiar-ai-agent/src/token_discipline.rs` — pure edit-form logic: `EditForm` (whole-file/search-replace/unified-diff), atomic anchor-based apply with named `AnchorDivergence`/`MalformedEdit` errors, idempotent-replay detection (anchor gone but replacement already present → no-op, not an error), and the targeted-edit worker-instruction text generator.
- `crates/familiar-ai-llm/src/token_discipline.rs` — pure bounded-result windowing: `bound_tool_result` (head+tail+elided-count+paging-handle), `file_read_requirement`, `slice_lines`.
- `crates/familiar-ai-storage/migrations/057_token_discipline.sql` — adds `edit_form_id`/`edit_form_version`/`truncation_config_id`/`truncation_config_version` to `usage_observations`, mirroring migration 043's compression-attribution pattern.
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/runtime_token_discipline.rs` — 6 tests: anchor-divergence rejection (file untouched), crash-replay identity, bounded command results with lossless worktree retention, retrieval through the paging handle via `read-file`, byte-for-byte defaults when disabled, and explicit-range requirement on oversized reads.

**Modified:** `raw_runtime.rs` (ReadFile schema gains optional `start_line`/`end_line`; `CallDisposition::Executed` gains `edit_form`), `daemon/agent_runtime.rs` (`SandboxedToolExecutor` wires targeted edits, bounded read/command results, `.familiar/tool-output/<call_id>.txt` lossless retention; `persist_run_outcome` takes `&TokenDisciplineConfig`), `core/config/agent_runtime.rs` (`TokenDisciplineConfig`, disabled by default, validated), `storage/repos/accounting.rs` + `migrate.rs` (new ledger columns, wired through), `docs/contracts/agent-loop.md` (new normative section), `config/default.toml`, plus mechanical updates to every existing `UsageObservation`/`SandboxedToolExecutor`/`persist_run_outcome` call site across daemon/mcp tests and `run.rs`.

**Acceptance criteria:** all six are met and covered by tests. One deliberate interpretation: the worker-instruction text (`targeted_edit_worker_instruction`) is implemented and tested but not wired into a live prompt-assembly call site — no such site exists yet in this codebase, since prompt/context construction is PRD-070, explicitly out of scope for PRD-072.

**Verification:** `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy` (no new warnings — two pre-existing ones in untouched files), and `cargo test` across every affected crate all pass. Full workspace `cargo check --all-targets` is clean. The only failure encountered was `cargo build`/`test` for the `familiar-ai-daemon` binary's default `tray` feature, which fails to link against a missing system library `libxdo` — pre-existing and unrelated to this PRD; worked around with `--no-default-features` for daemon test runs, per standard practice for this environment.
