{"review_id":"00001788454764715784-0001485283-000001-cycle-review-1","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:44d0b40222d4946e5c5efe3f9c059eb1f802e1bdc23e178e30a3e86532ffa2a3","findings":[{"finding_id":"batch-config-scope-mismatch","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Batch enablement is written per-repository but read from the global tier policy","claim":"`familiar-ai batch-review enable` mutates `repositories.<key>.review.tier_policy.{batch_risk_classes,batch_worker,max_batch_wait_ms}`, while `batch_auth` and `build_batch_reviewer` read only the top-level `config.review.tier_policy`. A repository enabled through the shipped CLI therefore never resolves a batch worker or credential, so `build_batch_reviewer` returns `None` and the coordinator silently runs the interactive reviewer even when the tier selection is `Batch` — the documented audited enablement path does not actually turn the feature on.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/cli/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":148,"end":176}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":560,"end":600}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":99927,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:477363d7733bc7795bec4ab633947af5c1870efe121f976b7121b63c84cf1bf0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Resolve the batch policy from the same repository-scoped `ReviewConfig` that `configured_tier_policy` and tier selection use (falling back to the global policy only when no repository override exists), and add a test that enables batch for a repository key and asserts `build_batch_reviewer` returns `Some`. Alternatively, have the CLI write the global policy and document that scoping explicitly.","remediation_note":null,"status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"poller-exits-when-batch-initially-disabled","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Batch poller exits permanently at daemon start when batch tiering is off, so later enablement has no lifecycle owner","claim":"`batch_review::run` calls `batch_auth(&config)` once and `return`s for the whole daemon lifetime when it is `None`. Because batch tiering defaults off, the poller task always exits at startup on a fresh install; if an operator then runs `batch-review enable`, submissions can be created by subsequent executions but nothing polls them, applies completions, or enforces the `max_batch_wait_ms` bound until the daemon is restarted — contradicting the requirement that the daemon owns batch lifecycle and that a PRD never sits in review-pending past the bound.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":636,"end":676}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/main.rs","range":{"start":358,"end":367}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":99927,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:477363d7733bc7795bec4ab633947af5c1870efe121f976b7121b63c84cf1bf0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Keep the poller task alive regardless of current configuration: tick unconditionally, re-evaluate `batch_auth` (and per-repository policy) on each tick, and no-op when nothing is configured — or re-spawn the poller when a config mutation enables batch tiering.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"submit-before-durable-record","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Provider batch is submitted before the durable row is written, so a crash in that window orphans and re-bills a batch","claim":"`BatchReviewAgent::submit` performs the provider `submit_message_batch` POST first and only then writes the `batch_reviews` row. A daemon crash (or a `BatchReviewRepository::submit` failure, which is mapped to `ReviewExecutionError::Agent` and drives a retry with a new `review_id`) between those two steps leaves a batch that the provider is processing and billing but that no durable state references; the re-driven attempt submits a second batch. This violates 'never loses a submitted batch' for exactly the crash window the acceptance criterion names.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":196,"end":236}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":99927,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:477363d7733bc7795bec4ab633947af5c1870efe121f976b7121b63c84cf1bf0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Write an intent row (e.g. state `submitting`, keyed by `review_id`, with the deterministic `custom_id`) before the POST and promote it to `submitted` with the returned `provider_batch_id` afterward; on resume, reconcile an unpromoted intent against the provider's batch list instead of blindly resubmitting.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"applied-before-disposition-persisted","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Completed result is marked `applied` before the disposition is persisted, discarding a paid-for review on any later failure","claim":"`consume_completed` calls `take_completed` (which transitions `completed` -> `applied` and returns the payload) before accounting, parsing, and long before the coordinator persists the cycle. If `record_accounting` fails, `parse_completed_result` rejects malformed reviewer output, or the coordinator's `save_cycle` fails, the durable row is already `applied`; a re-driven cycle that regenerates the same `review_id` hits the `BatchReviewState::Applied` arm, which returns a hard `Agent` error rather than re-reading the stored result or falling back, and later attempts pay for a second batch. The result is billed once and used zero times.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":330,"end":366}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":446,"end":480}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":99927,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:477363d7733bc7795bec4ab633947af5c1870efe121f976b7121b63c84cf1bf0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Retain `result_json` on transition to `applied` and have the `Applied` arm return the stored, re-parsed result (idempotent replay) instead of erroring; or defer the `completed` -> `applied` transition until the coordinator has durably saved the disposition, and treat unparseable batch output as an expiry-style fallback to the interactive tier rather than a bare agent error.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"no-coverage-for-daemon-owned-lifecycle","category":"test_gap","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Daemon-owned poller, resume path, and config-driven wiring are untested","claim":"Every test in `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/batch_review.rs` drives `BatchReviewAgent` directly with a hand-built `BatchReviewContext`. Nothing exercises `poll_once`/`run` (the component the acceptance criteria assign batch lifecycle ownership to), `resume_now`, or `build_batch_reviewer`/`batch_auth` reading real configuration. The two defects above — CLI-written per-repository policy never reaching `batch_auth`, and the poller exiting at startup — are exactly the failures this shape of test cannot catch, which is why they survive a green workspace test run.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":100,"end":128}},{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":676,"end":781}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":99927,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:477363d7733bc7795bec4ab633947af5c1870efe121f976b7121b63c84cf1bf0","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e9a2c877e124c192fbfcff557d2fd5178a89c0ad6331df58cfaf89d7ca5e4d77-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Add tests that (a) build a `Config` with batch enabled the way `batch-review enable` writes it and assert `build_batch_reviewer` returns `Some`, and (b) drive `poll_once` against a `wiremock` server plus an in-memory database, asserting it applies a completion and enforces expiry without any review cycle re-driving it.","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
