{"review_id":"00001788454764715784-0001485283-000001-cycle-review-2","reviewed_manifest_hash":"sha256:be435789602bff1bbbbf3841a11e07d3c9bb10574b711cf1dc6f16016702c4fc","findings":[{"finding_id":"batch-config-scope-mismatch","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Repository-scoped batch enablement is not read by the batch reviewer","claim":"Resolved in this revision. `batch_auth` and `build_batch_reviewer` now go through `resolved_tier_policy`, which looks up `config.repositories.<repository_key>.review.tier_policy` first and only falls back to the top-level `[review.tier_policy]`, so the policy `familiar-ai batch-review enable` writes under `repositories.<key>.review.tier_policy` is now the policy the reviewer resolves. A new integration test (`build_batch_reviewer_resolves_a_repository_scoped_enablement`) asserts both that a repository-scoped enablement resolves a batch reviewer with no top-level policy present, and that an unrelated repository key does not inherit it.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":540,"end":600}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e2db208b1a95243f6d343fa656ac856c92e9372cf8de01a196a41cc1f7ec8e2f","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":100000,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:33e19dd4d8f946dcee3247c008e726a2ed56e9caf9b757d9b39a051714d3d0e5","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e2db208b1a95243f6d343fa656ac856c92e9372cf8de01a196a41cc1f7ec8e2f-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"No further action required; the repository-scoped lookup and its regression test are in place.","status":"resolved","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"batch-cost-is-configured-interactive-rate","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"Batch accounting records a configured interactive-rate estimate, not provider-reported cost","claim":"`record_accounting` writes the batch observation with `provider_cost_lexical: None` and then, when a price is configured, calls `append_legacy_configured_estimate` using `config.execution_history.pricing[model]` — the same per-million rates used for interactive executions, with no batch discount applied — while labelling the rates blob `\"service_tier\": \"batch\"`. The durable `batch_reviews.provider_cost_lexical` column is likewise always written as `None` (`mark_completed(..., None)` in both `poll_or_expire` and `apply_batch_result`). The acceptance criterion requires the provider-reported cost with provider provenance so PRD-051 measures the actual discount rather than assuming a rate; what is recorded is a locally assumed rate carrying no provider provenance, and it assumes the interactive rate specifically.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":312,"end":400}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e2db208b1a95243f6d343fa656ac856c92e9372cf8de01a196a41cc1f7ec8e2f","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":100000,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:33e19dd4d8f946dcee3247c008e726a2ed56e9caf9b757d9b39a051714d3d0e5","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e2db208b1a95243f6d343fa656ac856c92e9372cf8de01a196a41cc1f7ec8e2f-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Record the provider's own reported batch cost (or, failing that, an explicitly batch-rated estimate) with provenance distinguishing it from an interactive-rate configured estimate: populate `batch_reviews.provider_cost_lexical` and the observation's `provider_cost_lexical` from provider data, and stop emitting an undiscounted interactive-rate estimate tagged as batch. Add a test asserting a batch observation's recorded cost differs from the interactive-rate computation for the same token counts.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"applied-state-strands-result-on-post-take-failure","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"high","blocking":false,"title":"take_completed flips the row to 'applied' before the result is parsed or dispositioned","claim":"`consume_completed` calls `take_completed`, which commits the `completed` -> `applied` transition, and only afterwards runs `record_accounting` and `parse_completed_result`. Any failure after that commit — or a daemon crash before the coordinator persists the resulting cycle — leaves the row permanently in `applied` with no consumer. A later re-drive matches the `BatchReviewState::Applied` arm of `review()` and returns a hard `ReviewExecutionError::Agent(\"... was already applied to a prior disposition\")` with no fallback to the interactive tier, unlike the expiry and member-error paths. The batch result is lost and the PRD cannot obtain a review at all.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":289,"end":310}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e2db208b1a95243f6d343fa656ac856c92e9372cf8de01a196a41cc1f7ec8e2f","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":100000,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:33e19dd4d8f946dcee3247c008e726a2ed56e9caf9b757d9b39a051714d3d0e5","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e2db208b1a95243f6d343fa656ac856c92e9372cf8de01a196a41cc1f7ec8e2f-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Only transition to `applied` once the result has actually been parsed and the disposition persisted (e.g. parse and record accounting first, then take/commit; or make the `applied` transition part of the same transaction that saves the cycle). Give the `Applied` arm a recovery path — fall back to the interactive tier with a durable reason instead of a permanent hard error — and add a test covering a completed batch whose payload fails to parse.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"poller-aborts-all-rows-on-one-row-failure","category":"correctness_defect","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"poll_once returns instead of continuing when one row's credential or client fails","claim":"Inside `poll_once`'s per-row loop, both the `AnthropicHttpClient::new` failure arm and the `EnvCredentialResolver.resolve(&auth)` failure arm `return` from the whole function rather than `continue` to the next row. Credential resolution is per-row (each repository may name a different batch worker and auth profile), so a single repository with a missing or unreadable credential aborts polling for every other pending batch on that tick, and does so on every subsequent tick as well.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":655,"end":690}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-workspace-advisory","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:e2db208b1a95243f6d343fa656ac856c92e9372cf8de01a196a41cc1f7ec8e2f","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":100000,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:33e19dd4d8f946dcee3247c008e726a2ed56e9caf9b757d9b39a051714d3d0e5","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-e2db208b1a95243f6d343fa656ac856c92e9372cf8de01a196a41cc1f7ec8e2f-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Replace the per-row `return`s with `continue` (keeping the warning log) so one repository's credential or client failure cannot stall polling for unrelated pending batches, and add a poller test with two pending rows where the first row's credential is unresolvable.","status":"open","supersedes":null},{"finding_id":"no-coverage-of-poller-or-coordinator-batch-path","category":"test_gap","severity":"medium","blocking":false,"title":"Daemon poller and coordinator-level batch result path are untested","claim":"The new integration tests drive `BatchReviewAgent::review` directly; nothing exercises `run`/`poll_once`/`apply_batch_result`/`resume_now`, which are the components the acceptance criteria assign daemon ownership of the batch lifecycle across restarts to. Separately, no test drives a batch-produced `ReviewResult` through `ReviewCoordinator`: the coordinator tests use `ParkingReviewer` (which only ever parks) and the plain fake `Reviewer`, so the fact that a batch result rewrites the reviewer `AgentObservation` (`adapter_id: \"anthropic-api-batch\"`, `agent_id: \"anthropic-api\"`, `provider: \"anthropic-api\"`) away from the assignment that `check_independence` was run against is never validated end to end.","evidence":[{"kind":"file_range","path":"crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/batch_review.rs","range":{"start":1,"end":30}},{"kind":"verification","check_id":"tests-green-crates","output":{"content_hash":"sha256:579e9bc243ebdea0e38b2d3e4bccbdade838c474e8a857712a94137add683621","media_type":"text/plain","byte_size":38343,"repository":"/home/trollboy/.local/state/familiar-ai/worktrees/drive-00001788454454062745-0001485283-000000/PRD-71","revision":"sha256:33e19dd4d8f946dcee3247c008e726a2ed56e9caf9b757d9b39a051714d3d0e5","storage_ref":"/home/trollboy/.local/share/familiar-ai/review-artifacts/sha256-579e9bc243ebdea0e38b2d3e4bccbdade838c474e8a857712a94137add683621-stdout","truncated":false,"omitted_bytes":0}}],"remediation":"Add a test that runs `poll_once` against a mock server plus durable rows (pending, ended-with-result, past-deadline) and asserts the resulting state transitions, and a coordinator test that supplies a batch-style `ReviewAgent` returning a `ReviewResult` with the rewritten reviewer observation, asserting it passes independence/validation and reaches the same disposition as an interactive result.","status":"open","supersedes":null}]}
