All green. Let's also run the full daemon crate's own test suite quickly to be safe (not just the batch_review file), and double check `git diff --stat` to confirm changes stayed within allowed paths.
All modified/new files are under `crates/`, matching the untracked baseline (I only touched `batch_review.rs` files — daemon src, storage repo, and daemon test — plus no other files). Format, clippy, and the relevant test suites all pass.
Both blocking findings are remediated within `crates/`, scope untouched otherwise:

1. **`batch-cost-is-configured-interactive-rate`** — `batch_cost_estimate()` now applies Anthropic's documented 50% batch discount to the configured per-token rate (the provider never returns a literal dollar figure for batch), tags the estimate's provenance as `"batch-rate-estimate"` distinct from the interactive configured-rate estimate, and both `mark_completed` call sites (`poll_or_expire` and `apply_batch_result`) now populate `batch_reviews.provider_cost_lexical` instead of always writing `None`. Added `batch_completion_records_a_batch_discounted_cost_distinct_from_interactive_rate`, which asserts the recorded cost is exactly half the undiscounted interactive-rate computation for identical tokens.

2. **`applied-state-strands-result-on-post-take-failure`** — replaced the atomic `take_completed` (which flipped `completed → applied` before parsing) with `peek_completed` (read-only) + `mark_applied` (commits only after `record_accounting` and `parse_completed_result` both succeed), so a parse/accounting failure leaves the row retryable in `completed` state rather than permanently stranded. Gave the `Applied` re-entry arm a durable recovery path (`mark_applied_reentry_fallback`, transitioning to `expired_fallback` with a recorded reason) instead of a hard, unrecoverable error. Added `completed_batch_with_unparseable_payload_never_strands_the_row_as_applied` and `applied_reentry_with_no_disposition_falls_back_to_interactive_with_a_durable_reason`.

Verification run locally: `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --no-default-features -D warnings`, and `cargo test` for `familiar-ai-core`, `familiar-ai-review`, `familiar-ai-agent`, `familiar-ai-storage`, and the daemon's `batch_review` integration tests — all pass (9/9 new/updated batch tests green). No commits made.
